Bug 534602 - Tolerate out-of-order AutoSync activity notifications. r=mkmelin

AutoSync activity bookkeeping assumed that every download and removal callback followed a priority-queue addition. Some IMAP paths can report completion without a tracked folder, causing the activity listener to dereference a missing sync item and throw.

Centralize creation of per-folder and per-server activity state, recover that state when a download starts without a preceding queue notification, preserve existing state across duplicate additions, and ignore untracked completion or removal notifications when there is no activity to update.

Keep canceled and completed processes in their terminal state during queue removal instead of attempting an invalid transition to completed. Add xpcshell coverage for untracked callbacks, recovered download state, cleanup, and canceled-process removal.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327482


